  "title": "Prunes with prosciutto",
  "description": "It is possible to cook the prosciutto prunes in a pan but it is better and easier to prepare them in the oven.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The prunes are wrapped with thin slices of Italian raw ham, the prosciutto. Easy to prepare and quick to cook!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":27612,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1714193370889} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 27612-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Prunes with prosciutto</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_1261.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\t<p>It is possible to cook the prosciutto prunes in a pan but it is better and easier to prepare them in the oven.</p>\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>7 thin slices prosciutto</li><li>20 prunes (pitted)</li><li>20 tooth picks</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li><p>Preheat the oven to 240°C (thermostat 8) and cover a baking tray with baking paper or aluminum foil.</p></li><li><p>Cut the prosciutto slices into thirds lengthwise.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_9734.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Wrap each prune with a slice of prosciutto.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_9738.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Secure with a wooden skewer (tooth pick).</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_9740.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Place the bites on the baking sheet and cook in the oven for 3-5 minutes.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_9748.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li><p>Serve immediately.</p><br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/10/IMG_1262.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Apéritifs</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": "Prunes are wrapped with thin slices of Italian cured ham, prosciutto. Easy, quick and delicious."
  },
